      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Ricciafluitans(001TC)/4386",
      "html": "<ul><li>Type: Moss (liverwort)</li><li>Origin: Cosmopolitan</li><li>Growth rate: Medium</li><li>Height: 3 - 5+ cm after two months in the tank</li><li>Light demand: Medium</li><li>CO2: Medium</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Ricciafluitans(001TC)/4386",
      "html": "<p>Riccia fluitans can be kept down by tying it to a stone with a piece of fishing line, but new shoots always grow towards the surface, so it may be necessary to prune it with scissors. It thrives best with added CO2 and in good growing conditions small oxygen bubbles form on the leaf tips.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Ricciafluitans(001TC)/4386",
      "html": "<p>Aquarium plant from tissue culture in closed cup. Japanese Takashi Amano has inspired many aquarium owners to keep the 1-5 cm tall cosmopolitic liverwort, Riccia fluitans, submerged. As a traditional floating plant it offers good protection for young fish.</p>"
    }
  ],
